/-!
# The actual eight-midpoint half-path actors are perfect

The original Cartan supplies a nontrivial odd diagonal image in the same
quotient coordinates as both injective path radicals. Each radical is
therefore generated by its commutators with that Cartan. Their literal join
is the actual half-path actor, which is consequently perfect and equals its
two-residual. The binary actor retains Cartan centralization; perfectness is
asserted only at eight-element midpoints. The source selects the geometry
and both intrinsic root classes without an additional marking premise.
-/

public noncomputable section
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
open Subgroup Theory.GroupTheory RankTwoAmalgam SimpleGraph SimpleGraph.Walk
open Theory.GroupTheory.AmalgamGraph Subgroup.CosetGeometry.RankTwo
